  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the vertices of a regular octagon that lie on a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be a point on the circle and let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math> denote the distance between the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> varies over the circle, then the maximum value of the product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math>, is",
    "image": null
  },
